sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Closing request A
    participant B as Closing request B
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Request advisory identity: api_idempotency_operations.operation_scope<br/>plus api_idempotency_operations.idempotency_key (not a row lock)
    A->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
    B->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
    Note over B,D: WAIT for A's publication transaction
    alt A commits invoice M
        A->>D: Freeze processed groups and invoice M<br/>Advance number and state_version, COMMIT
        D-->>B: Account lock granted
        alt B requests the same month M
            B->>D: Read the existing invoices.snapshot
            B->>D: COMMIT without publication writes
            Note over B,D: Same invoice number, no second credit debit
        else B requests the eligible next month
            B->>D: Validate ended month and closed predecessor<br/>Publish next invoice with next number, COMMIT
        else B requests a skipped or backward month
            B->>D: ROLLBACK, 409 billing_conflict
        end
    else A fails before publication commits
        A->>D: ROLLBACK snapshot, closure, group links and counters
        D-->>B: Account lock granted, no invoice M exists
        B->>D: Validate and publish its requested month normally
    end
    Note over A,D: CloseMonth uses customer and month as retry identity.<br/>It does not use the scoped command-key advisory lock.<br/>A lost committed response is resolved by the same-month retry.
